# Winter Agent OS V2 — repository hygiene
#
# TRACKED
#   code, config, knowledge, docs, tests, tools, handoff
#   dataset/candidate/**   reviewed templates + manifests: INPUTS to live-verified
#                          vision, so they belong in history (~20 MB)
#   dataset/truth_audit/{gather_live_20260914_115120,resource_cells_20260914_120027,
#                        hard_block_evidence}/**   named regression fixtures
#
# NOT TRACKED: bulk screenshot evidence
#   dataset/raw            ~1.0 GB rotating runtime captures
#   dataset/truth_audit rest ~80 MB of one-off audit crops
#
# Rationale: a checkpoint must stay fast and reviewable.  Screenshots are
# machine-local artefacts that retention already protects on disk, and the
# handoff records their absolute paths.  Committing ~1.1 GB of PNGs would make
# every checkpoint useless.
# Regenerate fixtures with: tools/capture_resource_tabs.py
#
# NOTE: image files are excluded by FILE pattern, never by excluding their
# parent directory — git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, which silently drops the regression fixtures.

# --- bulk evidence ---------------------------------------------------------
dataset/raw/**/*.png
dataset/raw/**/*.jpg
dataset/truth_audit/**/*.png
dataset/truth_audit/**/*.jpg
dataset/external/**/*.png
dataset/external/**/*.jpg

# tools/role_identity_probe.py writes its frames *and* a probe.json/ocr_tokens.json
# into dataset/raw/role_identity/<stamp>/.  The PNGs are covered above, but the
# JSONs are not, and a blanket dataset/raw/**/*.json rule is not an option: 43
# tracked label files live in that tree (dataset/raw/*/labels.json and friends) and
# they are curation inputs.  The curated copy of this evidence is kept under
# dataset/truth_audit/role_identity_*/ (tracked), so the raw one is redundant.
dataset/raw/role_identity/

# nested third-party clones: they are their own repositories and are
# REFERENCE_ONLY (see knowledge/external/projects.json).  Tracking them as plain
# directories made `git status` permanently dirty.
dataset/external/repositories/

# re-include the regression fixtures
!dataset/truth_audit/gather_live_20260914_115120/**/*.png
!dataset/truth_audit/resource_cells_20260914_120027/**/*.png
!dataset/truth_audit/hard_block_evidence/**/*.png
# the level-range and resource-availability findings rest on these frames
!dataset/truth_audit/level_probe_*/**/*.png
!dataset/truth_audit/resource_availability_*/**/*.png
# the map-vs-EVENT misclassification frame behind DISPATCH_NOT_PROVEN x28
!dataset/truth_audit/map_overlay_*/**/*.png
# the recall dialog + the frame proving the slot frees only on arrival, and the
# HUD frames the stamina gauge ROI was measured from
!dataset/truth_audit/march_recall_*/**/*.png
!dataset/truth_audit/hud_stamina_*/**/*.png
!dataset/truth_audit/free_stamina_*/**/*.png

# --- fixtures that a test file actually reads -------------------------------
# The rule above is a file pattern, so every one of these was silently untracked
# even though a test asserts against it: a fresh clone could not run
# tests/test_intel_pin_board.py, tests/test_beast_formation_page.py or
# tests/test_panel_redesign.py.  Re-include exactly what is read, nothing more.
# the pin-count fix (aspect floor 0.65 -> 0.5) is argued from these 4 frames
!dataset/truth_audit/intel_pin_board_*/**/*.png
# the formation page given a beast identity it does not display (0w)
!dataset/truth_audit/beast_formation_page_*/**/*.png
# the same page measured across the whole corpus: the four "identity" templates
# are crops of one control and the real target is only in the title bar
!dataset/truth_audit/beast_formation_identity_*/**/*.png
# the live run where OPEN_STAMINA_SOURCES finally executed, and the stamina
# refusal that verify_intel_hero_march_open used to record as a success
!dataset/truth_audit/stamina_check_live_*/**/*.png
# the two live runs that prove the camp panel now reports its stamina and that
# an unaffordable fight is refused before the tap instead of after it
!dataset/truth_audit/camp_panel_stamina_gate_*/**/*.png
# the alliance HOME page read as the GIFTS section (2026-09-15, two-layer defect)
!dataset/truth_audit/alliance_gifts_chain_*/**/*.png
# the live A/B that proves one decision per step (runtime made the step decision
# twice, so a stamina verifier judged an intel step)
!dataset/truth_audit/one_decision_per_step_*/**/*.png
# panel_redesign holds 69 frames / 34 MB, so only the 4 the test reads are
# re-included -- keep this list in sync with tests/test_panel_redesign.py
!dataset/truth_audit/panel_redesign/panel_meat_selected.png
!dataset/truth_audit/panel_redesign/panel_wood_reselect.png
!dataset/truth_audit/panel_redesign/panel_coal_selected.png
!dataset/truth_audit/panel_redesign/panel_iron_selected.png
# the only evidence of where the client states *which role is logged in*: the
# 领主档案 panel behind one tap on the avatar, plus the map frames either side of
# it.  tests/test_role_identity.py reads all three (one positive, two negatives),
# and they are ~1.9 MB total, so the directory is re-included whole rather than
# file by file -- a later frame added here would otherwise go silently untracked,
# which is the trap the note above describes.
!dataset/truth_audit/role_identity_*/**/*.png
# one live dispatch on 2026-09-16: the map frame with the march out (counter reads
# 1/2) and the frame 20 s later behind the resource dialog, where an empty ROI was
# being read as "idle" while that march was still marching.
# tests/test_march_count_idle.py reads both.
!dataset/truth_audit/march_counter_overlay_*/**/*.png
# 2026-09-16: making the daily entry point work end to end.  Two sets, both read by
# tests/test_daily_entry_template.py and nothing else:
#   * daily_entry_template_*  the live HOME frame the stale 2026-09-08 tap target
#     was re-registered from (old record d=18 against a gate of 8), and the overlay
#     showing the crop rectangle and the point the executor actually taps;
#   * daily_tasks_tab_*       the one bounded tap that revealed what is behind the
#     每日任务 tab (the panel lands on 章节任务; the daily tab showed activity 285
#     with nothing claimable), plus the panel frames either side of the Back that
#     leaves it.
!dataset/truth_audit/daily_entry_template_*/**/*.png
!dataset/truth_audit/daily_tasks_tab_*/**/*.png

# run_live.py debug dumps: body-detection retries leave these in the repo root
# (see 04_OPEN_ISSUES 0v).  Ignored rather than deleted -- they are the only
# record of what the unstable tap targets did.
out_*.png
out_intel_dbg/

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- editors / os ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- scratch ---------------------------------------------------------------
# pytest sandbox.  pytest.ini sets tmp_path_retention_policy=none, so tmp dirs
# are kept rather than deleted: this host aborts any shutil.rmtree over ~50
# files (SystemExit from the sandbox shim), and that aborted teardown corrupts
# fixture state and shows up as ~26 errors in unrelated files.  See the handoff
# issue 0bd.  Keeping them here means they stay out of git.  To override:
#   python -m pytest tests -q --basetemp=<dir>
tools/_pt_*/
.pytest_tmp_*/
*.tmp
.workbuddy-ai/handoff/.commit_message.txt
# command-output capture files: this machine cannot pipe stdout (no coreutils),
# so every probe writes out_*.txt and pages it back with Read
out.txt
out_*.txt
out_*.json
# MaaFramework's own logs and the per-run migration reports
learning/maa_logs/
learning/maa_migration/
dataset/evidence/maa_migration/
dataset/evidence/maa_live/
dataset/evidence/maa_probe_*.png
# probe crops.  These must NOT live under dataset/raw: that tree is the frame
# corpus and the corpus gate assumes every PNG in it is a full client frame.
# Measured 2026-09-15 -- 302x79 title crops in dataset/raw made every ROI fall
# outside the frame, so match_ccoeff could not run and SemanticROIVision.find
# raised ValueError instead of returning None.
dataset/probe_output/

# command-output capture files, the .xml / .md siblings of the out_*.txt rule
# above.  pytest's JUnit XML and the paged-back memory notes are written to the
# repo root by the same no-coreutils workaround, and they are scratch: the
# findings they carry are meant to be distilled into .workbuddy-ai/handoff/,
# not versioned.  The r17 batch (out_junit_r17.xml, out_memory_{entry,addendum}_r17.md)
# slipped into history before this rule existed and stays tracked -- rule 20 of
# 00_MASTER_RULES forbids deleting them without an itemised confirmation.
# Ignored rather than deleted: same rationale as the out_*.txt block.
out_*.xml
out_*.md
# probe crop dumps written by the daily-entry / role-identity probes.  Same
# class as dataset/probe_output/ above, and equally machine-local.
out_crop_*/

# --- credentials -----------------------------------------------------------
# The repository is PUBLIC (https://github.com/hongweixiong0-star/winter-agent-os-v2),
# so anything here would be a disclosure, not just an untidy commit.  These rules are
# the first line; `tools/scan_public_repo.py` is the second and it fails the check
# whether or not a file is ignored, so a rule that stops matching cannot hide the file
# it was protecting.  Patterns are deliberately generic (`token*`, `session*`) and
# anchored-free: a stray `*.key` anywhere in the tree is not worth the tidiness of a
# narrow rule.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
secrets*
credentials*
token*
cookie*
session*
# ...except the game's own "session disconnected" popup.  `session*` above is a
# credential rule, and this client really does draw a session-dropped dialog, so four
# domain fixtures match it: the two templates, their manifest and the replay labels.
# Without these lines a future edit to them would be silently ignored -- the failure
# mode that makes an over-broad ignore rule dangerous rather than merely tidy.
!dataset/candidate/session_disconnected/
!dataset/candidate/session_disconnected_manifest.json
!tests/replay/session_disconnected_labels.json
# WorkBuddy's connector cache sits inside the project when the desktop app is opened
# from here; it holds OAuth material for the connected GitHub / mail accounts.
.workbuddy/connectors/
.workbuddy/plugins/
.workbuddy/blobs/
